)ATTR DEFAULT(@}_)
 @ TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(WHITE)
 } TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(GREEN)
 { TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(TURQ)
 _ TYPE(INPUT)  INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(RED)    CAPS(ON) JUST(LEFT)
 ! TYPE(OUTPUT) INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(YELLOW) CAPS(OFF) JUST(LEFT)
)BODY
@HELP: Status Panel -- the ST Command           !ISFHMSG                      }
@COMMAND INPUT ===>_ISFHCMD                                                  }
}
@  ST}[classes] [name]
}
{  classes  }Up to 6 job classes, written right after ST without a blank:
}            STA shows the jobs of class A, STAB those of A and B. TSO
}            users, started tasks and the print queue have no class to go
}            by and are left out. ST alone shows every class.
{  name     }A job name. * stands for any number of characters, % for one:
}            ST IEB* shows the jobs whose names start with IEB, ST IEB
}            only those named IEB. ST alone shows every name.
}
}  Examples:
{    ST          }every job you may see
{    STA         }the jobs of class A
{    ST TBR*     }the jobs whose names start with TBR
{    STAB HERC%1 }the jobs of class A or B named HERC, any character, 1
}
}  The classes and the name stay until the next ST. A PREFIX set before
}  (a command on every panel) applies as well: a job must match both. So
}  does a DEST limit.
}
}  Enter: next topic   PF7: Status panel help   PF3: back to SDSF
)PROC
  &ISFHPFK = .PFKEY
  &ZCONT = ISFHSTA
  &ZUP = ISFHST
)END
